-- title:
--   Origin cosets: [a]P+[b]Q meets the origin iff b=0
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative local Noetherian ring that is complete with respect to its maximal ideal, let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $T$ which is elliptic, and let $G$ be a `RelativeGroupLaw` on the structure morphism `projModelStrCR W` of the projective model of $W$, that is, a group structure on the sections $\{\varphi : Y \to \operatorname{Proj} \mid \varphi \text{ over } t\}$ for every $t : Y \to \operatorname{Spec} T$, with unit, inverse, associativity and compatibility with base change. Two hypotheses tie $G$ down: there is a family of bijections $ev$ between sections over $\operatorname{Spec} F$, for fields $F$ over $T$, and the points of the affine base change $W_F$, additive for $G$ and equivariant for Galois twisting (`IsPointsEval`); and the unit section $G.\mathrm{one}(\mathbb{1})$ is the origin-chart section attached to some ring homomorphism $\chi : \mathrm{OriginChartRing}\,W \to T$ (its underlying morphism factors as $\operatorname{Spec}\chi$ followed by `originChartι`) with $\chi(\mathrm{xOverY}\,W) = \chi(\mathrm{zOverY}\,W) = 0$. Let $q$ be prime, and let $P, Q$ be sections over the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} T$ such that: $P$ reduces to the origin via some $\chi_P$, meaning $P$ is the origin-chart section of $\chi_P$ and both `originParam` $\chi_P$ and `originW` $\chi_P$ lie in the maximal ideal; $Q$ satisfies $[q]Q = G.\mathrm{one}(\mathbb{1})$ for the iterated multiplication `nsmul`; and no ring homomorphism $\chi$ exhibits $Q$ as reducing to the origin in this sense. Then, for natural numbers $a$ and $b$ with $b < q$, the section $\mathrm{linComb}\,G\,P\,Q\,a\,b = G.\mathrm{mul}([a]P, [b]Q)$ reduces to the origin for some $\chi$ if and only if $b = 0$.
--
--   This is the statement that, in the coset decomposition of the $q$-torsion generated by a formal-group section $P$ and a section $Q$ whose reduction is non-trivial, exactly the cosets with vanishing $Q$-component meet the origin; equivalently, reduction modulo the maximal ideal separates the $\langle Q\rangle$-components. It supplies one of the two hypotheses used in [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.isDrinfeldBasis_iff_nsmul_eq_one_and_nthSeries_eq_mul_prod_of_reducesToOrigin`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.isDrinfeldBasis_iff_nsmul_eq_one_and_nthSeries_eq_mul_prod_of_reducesToOrigin) and in [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.torsionIdeal_le_basisDivisor_of_nsmul_eq_one_of_nthSeries_eq_mul_prod`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.torsionIdeal_le_basisDivisor_of_nsmul_eq_one_of_nthSeries_eq_mul_prod), where the divisor of the $q$-division series at the origin is computed for an ordinary Drinfeld basis.
